WEBVTT

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:07.457
In this video, we'll look at the media library, the site settings, and how to make your own share card.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.773
The Media tab, at the top, holds the site's shared images.

00:00:12.773 --> 00:00:17.290
Upload adds one, and Search finds one by its file name.

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:21.207
Let's upload a practice image, and find it.

00:00:25.104 --> 00:00:27.474
Click an image to select it.

00:00:27.474 --> 00:00:33.824
Copy copies its address, Download saves it, and Delete selected removes it.

00:00:34.541 --> 00:00:41.091
An image you upload inside an FAQ's answer is stored with that FAQ, so it doesn't appear here.

00:00:41.091 --> 00:00:48.755
To reuse an image from Media in an answer, copy its address here, then use Insert from URL in the image block.

00:00:48.755 --> 00:00:56.141
And delete an image from Media only when you're sure no page uses it, or that page shows a broken picture.

00:00:56.696 --> 00:01:01.456
This practice image isn't used anywhere, so we'll delete it.

00:01:02.163 --> 00:01:06.616
Site Settings change the whole site at once, at the next rebuild.

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:08.877
Most of them never need touching.

00:01:08.877 --> 00:01:14.083
If you do change something, change one thing at a time, then check the site.

00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:16.353
Typography and fonts.

00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:24.237
The fonts themselves are fixed to the site's faces, but sizes and line spacing can move within set limits.

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:29.071
Each hint gives the default value, so you can always put it back.

00:01:29.784 --> 00:01:34.271
Colours and theme has one choice: comfortable, or high contrast.

00:01:34.271 --> 00:01:36.584
Both are checked for readability.

00:01:37.312 --> 00:01:42.394
AI and search crawlers lets you allow or block each AI company's bots.

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:49.363
Some learn from the site, and others fetch pages to answer people's questions, with a link back.

00:01:49.363 --> 00:01:55.752
Allowing all of them helps CCS's work reach people who ask AI tools about Indian policy.

00:01:56.465 --> 00:02:00.132
The content guide is a quick reference for editors.

00:02:00.132 --> 00:02:02.145
Nothing in it needs editing.

00:02:02.858 --> 00:02:11.969
Every page gets a share card automatically: the picture shown when someone posts its link on WhatsApp, LinkedIn or X.

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:15.473
To make your own, open /tools/og on the site.

00:02:15.473 --> 00:02:21.858
Type the eyebrow, headline and button text, pick a colour, and click Download PNG.

00:02:22.653 --> 00:02:28.958
Then upload it to the Share image field, at the top of that FAQ, video or topic.

00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:35.579
For the home, about, glossary, search and AI pages, use Site Settings, Share images.

00:02:35.579 --> 00:02:41.333
Note that WhatsApp and LinkedIn remember a link's old card for some days.

00:02:42.053 --> 00:02:44.210
This is that Share images page.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.453
Leave a box empty to keep the card that's made automatically.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:57.580
Next, and last: what happens on its own, what to do when something goes wrong, and cleaning up after practice.
